        "original_id": "181e84c6-450f-5b3a-9557-f70cf2095e59",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Archie Andrews, John L. Goldwater, Bob Montana, Vic Bloom, Fiona Staples\n- Organizations: Archie Comics\n- Products: Archie, Archie Andrews radio series, The Archie Show, Archie's Weird Mysteries, Pep Comics, North 40, DV8: Gods and Monsters, T.H.U.N.D.E.R. Agents, Saga\n- Characters: Archie Andrews, Comet\n- Topics: comic books, comic book artists\n\nFacts:\n- Comet is a fictional character that first appeared in Pep Comics #1 in January 1940.\n- Archie Andrews was created in 1941 by publisher John L. Goldwater and artist Bob Montana in collaboration with writer Vic Bloom.\n- Archie Andrews is the main character in an American comic book series published by Archie Comics.\n- Archie Andrews is also featured in the long-running Archie Andrews radio series, the syndicated comic strip, The Archie Show, and Archie's Weird Mysteries.\n- Archie is an ongoing comic book series, also known as Archie Comics, that features the Archie Comics character Archie Andrews.\n- Fiona Staples is a Canadian comic book artist known for work on North 40, DV8: Gods and Monsters, T.H.U.N.D.E.R. Agents, Archie, and Saga.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
